{
  "dom_id": "step-q130764",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "A  fair octahedral die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $8$ is rolled $25$ times. What is the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times we get a number divisible by $3.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=25$ rolls\n\n- the probability of getting a number divisible by $3$ (i.e., a $3$ or a $6$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(25,\\frac{1}{4}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of times we get a number divisible by $3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
